 "notes": "Controller: IK-based Cartesian servoing of the grasp site with a fixed palm-down orientation, with yaw aligned to the cube yaw (modulo 90\u00b0). The yaw candidate is chosen at the start by offline IK feasibility at the pick and place poses. State machine: hover above the target cube, descend, close slowly, lift, carry at a hover height chosen per layout (0.91 to 0.98 m, as high as IK reaches), descend onto the destination cube using the measured cube-in-hand offset, release slowly (closure ramp over about 2.4 s), then retreat. It re-checks the result: if the cube is dropped, slips out of the hand, or ends up off the destination, it re-plans and retries while t < 18 s. Practice results were about 90% (37/40 on seeds 100000-100039; about 83% on seeds 100040-100077 before the slow-release change). Known weaknesses: weak 2-point grasps when the cube yaw is near 45\u00b0 relative to the hand; a cube sometimes slips during carry; cubes close to the body (x < 0.18) are hard to reach and the arm can sweep cubes off the table; retries can fling cubes when the IK target is near the workspace edge; the carry phase has no collision avoidance for other cubes beyond hover height.",
